1
00:01:04,800 --> 00:01:08,080
[Fragments of Truth]

2
00:01:08,080 --> 00:01:09,600
[Episode 21]

3
00:01:20,480 --> 00:01:21,400
Yes, speaking.

4
00:01:22,270 --> 00:01:23,240
All right.
Go ahead.

5
00:01:30,480 --> 00:01:31,880
Understood.
Thank you.

6
00:01:36,480 --> 00:01:36,990
Captain.

7
00:01:37,320 --> 00:01:40,320
Han Ning asked me
to investigate Sun Jiahao's connections

8
00:01:41,120 --> 00:01:42,680
at the hospital that treated Xiao Ting.

9
00:01:43,840 --> 00:01:44,630
What did you find?

10
00:01:44,630 --> 00:01:47,480
Sun Jiahao and Fan Zhichang,

11
00:01:47,480 --> 00:01:49,840
Rennian Hospital's director
and former OB-GYN chief,

12
00:01:49,840 --> 00:01:50,880
are uncle and nephew.

13
00:01:51,040 --> 00:01:51,990
Fan Zhichang

14
00:01:53,880 --> 00:01:55,350
was Han Shuang's supervisor back then.

15
00:01:57,680 --> 00:02:00,270
Sun Jiahao is Fan Zhichang's nephew.

16
00:02:00,680 --> 00:02:01,880
He took his mother's surname.

17
00:02:02,120 --> 00:02:04,320
His father died many years ago.

18
00:02:04,320 --> 00:02:05,790
His name was Fan Zhicheng.

19
00:02:05,790 --> 00:02:06,840
He was Fan Zhichang's younger brother.

20
00:02:08,280 --> 00:02:09,000
Tell Han Ning immediately.

21
00:02:09,320 --> 00:02:09,880
Have him keep investigating.
Yes, Captain.

22
00:02:30,670 --> 00:02:31,280
Xiao Ning.

23
00:02:31,630 --> 00:02:32,560
Hello.

24
00:02:33,230 --> 00:02:34,670
Hello.

25
00:02:35,200 --> 00:02:35,910
Who is this?

26
00:02:35,910 --> 00:02:37,280
Officer He from our division.

27
00:02:38,790 --> 00:02:39,790
Let's shake hands again.

28
00:02:39,790 --> 00:02:40,880
Come on, one more time.

29
00:02:40,880 --> 00:02:41,480
Welcome.

30
00:02:43,600 --> 00:02:44,480
Xiao Ning.

31
00:02:45,910 --> 00:02:47,280
I never expected this.

32
00:02:47,280 --> 00:02:48,880
You've grown

33
00:02:50,040 --> 00:02:51,110
into a fine young man.

34
00:02:52,390 --> 00:02:52,720
By the way,

35
00:02:53,790 --> 00:02:54,630
I still remember.

36
00:02:55,000 --> 00:02:55,880
When you were little,

37
00:02:56,200 --> 00:02:58,110
your sister brought you to the hospital.

38
00:02:59,110 --> 00:02:59,790
You still remember that?

39
00:03:00,480 --> 00:03:02,110
My sister was afraid her supervisor
would scold her,

40
00:03:02,110 --> 00:03:03,160
so she hid me in a ward.

41
00:03:04,910 --> 00:03:06,720
Your sister was a fine colleague.

42
00:03:07,440 --> 00:03:09,000
She was my most promising junior.

43
00:03:13,510 --> 00:03:14,630
I'm very sorry

44
00:03:15,320 --> 00:03:16,200
about what happened to her.

45
00:03:18,000 --> 00:03:18,560
Come in.
Come in.
Sit down.
Please.

46
00:03:26,720 --> 00:03:28,070
Did you come today

47
00:03:28,880 --> 00:03:32,720
because there's progress in her case?

48
00:03:33,110 --> 00:03:33,830
And your surname is...?

49
00:03:34,720 --> 00:03:35,480
Officer He.
Here.

50
00:03:35,950 --> 00:03:36,790
All right.
Thank you.

51
00:03:38,880 --> 00:03:39,510
Here's the situation.

52
00:03:39,720 --> 00:03:40,910
We came today

53
00:03:40,910 --> 00:03:43,000
to ask you, Director Fan,

54
00:03:43,390 --> 00:03:46,000
about a patient named Xiao Ting
from seven years ago.

55
00:03:46,070 --> 00:03:47,510
Do you remember her?

56
00:03:59,280 --> 00:04:00,350
Xiao Ting?

57
00:04:01,670 --> 00:04:02,280
Oh.

58
00:04:02,280 --> 00:04:05,110
I saw too many people
at the hospital every day.

59
00:04:06,200 --> 00:04:08,070
I couldn't remember everyone.

60
00:04:12,110 --> 00:04:13,720
She had a medical record, right?

61
00:04:15,390 --> 00:04:17,590
That's precisely what's strange.

62
00:04:18,270 --> 00:04:19,120
This young woman

63
00:04:19,120 --> 00:04:21,070
was admitted to your department
for a threatened miscarriage.

64
00:04:21,070 --> 00:04:22,470
She stayed here.

65
00:04:22,800 --> 00:04:24,120
But we can't find her medical record

66
00:04:24,120 --> 00:04:25,270
anywhere.

67
00:04:25,920 --> 00:04:26,320
Oh.

68
00:04:27,070 --> 00:04:28,270
That's impossible.

69
00:04:29,070 --> 00:04:30,920
Could you be mistaken?

70
00:04:32,000 --> 00:04:32,800
No, we're not.

71
00:04:33,000 --> 00:04:34,390
My sister cared for this patient.

72
00:04:37,920 --> 00:04:39,590
If that's the case,

73
00:04:41,120 --> 00:04:43,000
there may be another possibility.

74
00:04:45,120 --> 00:04:45,920
What possibility?

75
00:04:51,030 --> 00:04:51,710
Well...

76
00:04:53,120 --> 00:04:56,000
The medical staff caring for her
may have altered the record.

77
00:04:56,270 --> 00:04:56,920
That would explain

78
00:04:57,710 --> 00:04:59,000
why the record is missing.

79
00:05:00,800 --> 00:05:01,560
My sister

80
00:05:01,830 --> 00:05:02,800
altered the medical record?

81
00:05:04,270 --> 00:05:04,630
Uh...

82
00:05:05,830 --> 00:05:06,880
I only mean

83
00:05:07,030 --> 00:05:09,030
it's theoretically possible.

84
00:05:09,800 --> 00:05:11,680
But I believe your sister was good.

85
00:05:11,680 --> 00:05:12,880
She wouldn't do such a thing.

86
00:05:14,710 --> 00:05:15,320
Please think again.

87
00:05:15,710 --> 00:05:16,590
Do you remember anything else?

88
00:05:32,630 --> 00:05:33,440
Take two.

89
00:05:34,120 --> 00:05:35,030
Here, two pills.
Mm.

90
00:05:42,270 --> 00:05:43,070
Well.

91
00:05:47,510 --> 00:05:48,470
Let's do this.

92
00:05:48,880 --> 00:05:49,710
As for me,

93
00:05:50,630 --> 00:05:53,710
I'll check my old work notes again.

94
00:05:54,470 --> 00:05:56,470
If I remember anything,

95
00:05:57,120 --> 00:05:58,440
I'll contact you.

96
00:06:01,470 --> 00:06:02,270
Okay.

97
00:06:07,070 --> 00:06:08,830
Honey, see them out.

98
00:06:09,470 --> 00:06:10,590
I'm terribly sorry.

99
00:06:11,800 --> 00:06:13,590
My husband has been unwell lately.

100
00:06:14,320 --> 00:06:15,710
His condition is unstable,

101
00:06:16,120 --> 00:06:17,200
better some days and worse on others.

102
00:06:17,830 --> 00:06:18,630
Oh.

103
00:06:19,240 --> 00:06:19,680
Sorry.

104
00:06:20,390 --> 00:06:21,440
As for Mr. Fan's condition...

105
00:06:21,440 --> 00:06:22,920
Let me give you a stamp.

106
00:06:24,360 --> 00:06:24,800
Excuse me.

107
00:06:27,120 --> 00:06:28,880
You already have so many stamps.

108
00:06:29,030 --> 00:06:30,070
They look nice.

109
00:06:42,240 --> 00:06:42,680
Uncle He.

110
00:06:55,880 --> 00:06:58,240
It appears
Director Fan will have to come with us.

111
00:07:12,030 --> 00:07:13,630
Let go of me!

112
00:07:38,680 --> 00:07:39,470
Let go of me!

113
00:07:41,120 --> 00:07:42,270
Let go of me!

114
00:07:45,590 --> 00:07:47,270
Let go of me!

115
00:07:49,920 --> 00:07:51,320
Let go of me!

116
00:07:52,030 --> 00:07:53,070
We're out of Ringer's solution.

117
00:07:53,070 --> 00:07:54,070
Go prepare some.

118
00:07:59,200 --> 00:08:00,000
Let go of me!

119
00:08:01,270 --> 00:08:02,070
Stay calm.

120
00:08:02,710 --> 00:08:03,590
Listen to me.

121
00:08:04,710 --> 00:08:05,830
I made some adjustments.

122
00:08:06,390 --> 00:08:07,120
You'll be fine.

123
00:08:18,880 --> 00:08:19,680
Trust me.

124
00:08:20,120 --> 00:08:21,150
For the foreseeable future,

125
00:08:21,270 --> 00:08:22,470
don't do anything reckless

126
00:08:22,710 --> 00:08:24,120
or let them notice you.

127
00:08:24,390 --> 00:08:25,880
Leave the rest to me.

128
00:08:26,120 --> 00:08:27,000
Do you understand?

129
00:08:32,120 --> 00:08:32,920
Can you swim?

130
00:08:35,990 --> 00:08:36,680
Answer me.
Can you swim?

131
00:08:38,320 --> 00:08:38,750
Yes.

132
00:08:39,710 --> 00:08:41,680
I grew up beside the Dongjiang River.

133
00:08:42,710 --> 00:08:44,710
All wastewater here
drains into a holding pond

134
00:08:44,870 --> 00:08:45,800
connected to the river.

135
00:08:48,110 --> 00:08:48,920
When the time comes, I'll find a way

136
00:08:49,200 --> 00:08:50,280
to get you out through there.

137
00:09:06,710 --> 00:09:07,110
Sis.

138
00:09:07,470 --> 00:09:08,320
Here.
Take this.

139
00:09:12,920 --> 00:09:13,560
It's a whistle.

140
00:09:13,830 --> 00:09:14,750
Why are you giving me this?

141
00:09:15,320 --> 00:09:16,590
Winter is almost here.

142
00:09:16,680 --> 00:09:17,870
It gets dark early.

143
00:09:17,870 --> 00:09:19,040
Keep this with you.

144
00:09:19,470 --> 00:09:20,710
If you meet a bad person,

145
00:09:20,920 --> 00:09:21,990
blow it.

146
00:09:22,040 --> 00:09:23,640
It'll scare them away.

147
00:09:24,070 --> 00:09:25,440
What if they aren't scared?

148
00:09:25,990 --> 00:09:27,280
I'll hear it too.

149
00:09:27,470 --> 00:09:29,320
Then I'll hurry over to protect you.

150
00:09:32,920 --> 00:09:33,750
Then...

151
00:09:34,870 --> 00:09:37,040
What if you don't hear it?

152
00:09:37,710 --> 00:09:39,200
I'll still hear it.

153
00:09:39,520 --> 00:09:41,400
All right.
I understand.

154
00:09:59,870 --> 00:10:00,680
Han Ning.

155
00:10:01,110 --> 00:10:02,830
Why did you bring him here?

156
00:10:05,710 --> 00:10:07,400
I found Sun Jiahao's seal design

157
00:10:07,400 --> 00:10:08,440
on his son's clothes.

158
00:10:08,830 --> 00:10:09,990
They're uncle and nephew.

159
00:10:09,990 --> 00:10:11,110
It could have been a gift.

160
00:10:12,680 --> 00:10:14,800
Even if the seal
weren't personal property,

161
00:10:14,830 --> 00:10:17,680
given the time
since Sun Jiahao's death,

162
00:10:18,320 --> 00:10:20,520
this seal could only have been

163
00:10:20,520 --> 00:10:21,470
brought here after he died.
What does that mean?

164
00:10:22,470 --> 00:10:24,320
That they're uncle and nephew.

165
00:10:25,800 --> 00:10:28,280
That he was involved
in Sun Jiahao's death.

166
00:10:29,710 --> 00:10:31,400
But that's not direct evidence.

167
00:10:31,400 --> 00:10:33,320
At his age, who could he kill?

168
00:10:33,320 --> 00:10:34,680
If the chief asks,

169
00:10:34,830 --> 00:10:36,040
maybe we should release him.

170
00:10:36,750 --> 00:10:37,920
There's no turning back now.

171
00:10:40,350 --> 00:10:40,710
Fang Xin.

172
00:10:40,870 --> 00:10:41,750
Go calm Mr. Fan down.

173
00:10:42,200 --> 00:10:42,590
Gao Yuan.

174
00:10:42,950 --> 00:10:43,990
Go hold off Mr. Fan's wife.

175
00:10:44,870 --> 00:10:45,110
Okay.

176
00:10:53,070 --> 00:10:53,590
Captain Ren.

177
00:10:54,590 --> 00:10:55,320
This

178
00:10:55,520 --> 00:10:56,870
was my decision alone.

179
00:10:57,200 --> 00:10:58,640
If anything happens,
I'll take full responsibility.

180
00:10:59,520 --> 00:11:00,870
What makes you think you can?

181
00:11:01,320 --> 00:11:02,590
Now you're afraid?

182
00:11:07,320 --> 00:11:08,320
How sure are you?

183
00:11:10,070 --> 00:11:11,590
Something is definitely wrong
with Fan Zhichang.

184
00:11:12,110 --> 00:11:12,710
As for

185
00:11:12,950 --> 00:11:13,870
how deeply he was involved,

186
00:11:14,520 --> 00:11:15,230
I can't say yet.

187
00:11:17,990 --> 00:11:18,870
Then right now,

188
00:11:19,280 --> 00:11:20,710
you need only consider two things.

189
00:11:21,440 --> 00:11:21,830
First:

190
00:11:22,520 --> 00:11:24,280
What clue do you want from him?

191
00:11:24,590 --> 00:11:24,870
Second:

192
00:11:25,640 --> 00:11:26,520
How will you get it?

193
00:11:30,320 --> 00:11:31,710
You have 24 hours at most.

194
00:11:31,990 --> 00:11:32,870
Don't waste time.

195
00:11:33,320 --> 00:11:34,110
Yes.

196
00:12:11,070 --> 00:12:13,130
♪I stand in a fire-tempered jungle♪

197
00:12:13,130 --> 00:12:15,080
♪Withered leaves fall
as my strength runs dry♪

198
00:12:15,080 --> 00:12:16,990
♪Dust swirls as I clench my fists♪

199
00:12:16,990 --> 00:12:18,790
♪I strategize, my faith my armor♪

200
00:12:18,790 --> 00:12:21,130
♪My defiance spills onto concrete♪

201
00:12:21,130 --> 00:12:23,560
♪Even thick fog can't hide
my clear gaze♪

202
00:12:26,700 --> 00:12:28,610
♪Let neon turn to thorns♪

203
00:12:28,610 --> 00:12:30,500
♪Flying low as the stars shift and turn♪

204
00:12:30,500 --> 00:12:32,450
♪Escape the maze,
transcend the challenge♪

205
00:12:32,450 --> 00:12:34,570
♪The meter starts, breaking the silence♪

206
00:12:34,610 --> 00:12:36,580
♪A beam cuts through
a crack in the wall♪

207
00:12:36,580 --> 00:12:38,740
♪This rhythm and noise
echo through the streets♪

208
00:12:42,340 --> 00:12:45,820
♪Don't be afraid. No one will answer♪

209
00:12:45,820 --> 00:12:49,190
♪Why is that child crying?♪

210
00:12:49,420 --> 00:12:51,890
♪The shrinking scar on my arm♪

211
00:12:51,890 --> 00:12:53,510
♪Means I've grown up♪

212
00:12:53,510 --> 00:12:56,660
♪You can trust me when I say that♪

213
00:12:56,660 --> 00:13:00,140
♪The wound still aches♪

214
00:13:00,550 --> 00:13:04,900
♪Like a biting winter♪

215
00:13:04,900 --> 00:13:08,170
♪But a spark still glows♪

